Subject: [PATCH 17/18] docs: Super VL's memory and speed on one GB10 against
 1.0.12; the older figures named as 1.0.12's

The recipe gives the memory this build admits with (72.93 GiB with the tower and 0.40 GiB a stream at the default
window, 1.39 GiB at 131,072) and a paired table against 1.0.12 built from source on the same GB10: drafted decode on
counting, prose, code and an image, counting with "draft": false, 1 to 8 concurrent streams together and cold prompts
of 2,048 to 16,384 tokens, with how each was run. The eight-prompt table, the two-GB10 rows and checkpoint against
full are 1.0.12's and now say so, here and in the quantization guide.
---
 docs/quantization.md                  |  9 ++---
 docs/recipes/nemotron-3.5-super-vl.md | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 44 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

