 ## Exactness and speed
 
-Served on GB10s at a 16,384-token window, the eight release prompts at 256 tokens each, every cell held in both
-precisions: drafted replies equal `"draft": false` (greedy, seeded sampled, thinking on), 2 and 4 concurrent streams
-equal their solo runs, and three-turn chats with regenerate, edit and delete equal a cache-off server's replies.
+On one GB10, against 1.0.12 built from source on the same machine, in `checkpoint`: every reply below was 1.0.12's
+tokens (counting, multilingual and six language prompts were also sent with `"draft": false` and gave the same
+tokens), and concurrent streams equalled their solo runs. Decode was served with
+`--vision --context 131072`, each prompt run once to warm up and three times measured (median shown), for 256 tokens
+(400 counting). Each cold prompt ran alone on a server with `--context 18432 --prompt-cache-gib 0`, after the GPU
+cooled to 75 °C, three times for 32 tokens (median shown).
+
+| Measure | 1.0.12 | Now |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Counting from 1 to 1,000, MTP drafts | 75.86 tok/s | 92.72 tok/s (+22.2%) |
+| A short story, MTP drafts | 29.28 tok/s | 34.52 tok/s (+17.9%) |
+| A Python function, MTP drafts | 43.91 tok/s | 51.42 tok/s (+17.1%) |
+| Describing an image's shapes, MTP drafts | 59.88 tok/s | 71.88 tok/s (+20.0%) |
+| Counting, `"draft": false` | 18.49 tok/s | 21.44 tok/s (+16.0%) |
+| 1, 2, 4 and 8 concurrent streams, together | 43.93, 41.05, 57.10, 68.69 tok/s | 51.46, 47.32, 64.97, 87.57 tok/s |
+| Cold 2,048-token prompt | 1.216 s | 0.905 s (−25.6%) |
+| Cold 8,192-token prompt | 4.447 s | 3.078 s (−30.8%) |
+| Cold 16,384-token prompt | 13.254 s | 8.958 s (−32.4%) |
+
+This build drafted counting in 31 rounds; fresh servers of an earlier build of these changes took 30 rounds in 6 of 7
+boots (95.6 to 95.9 tok/s). Six prompts in English, Spanish, French, German, Italian and Japanese drafted 10.9% to
+18.5% faster. Every 16,384-token prompt waited 4 to 6 s at the engine's heat gate inside its prefill, in both builds.
+On a second GB10, a harness of ten greedy prompts (an image among them) and sampled code and prose gave 1.0.12's
+tokens, drafted replies equal to `"draft": false`, concurrent streams equal to their solo runs and resumed prompts
+equal to fresh ones.
+
+1.0.12, served on GB10s at a 16,384-token window, the eight release prompts at 256 tokens each, held every cell in
+both precisions: drafted replies equal `"draft": false` (greedy, seeded sampled, thinking on), 2 and 4 concurrent
+streams equal their solo runs, and three-turn chats with regenerate, edit and delete equal a cache-off server's
+replies. Its speeds, not measured again since:
 
